  "problem": "Which of the following probabilities could be approximated using the normal approximation of the binomial distribution?\n\nI. The probability that a fair coin lands on tails $5$ times out of $8$ coin flips.\n\nII. The probability of choosing $5$ men in a neighborhood with $40$ adults if the probability that a randomly selected adult is a man is $0.55.$\n\nIII. The probability that a golf player makes less than $3$ putts in $15$ shots at the same hole if the probability of making a putt in each shot is $0.3.$",
